# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
**/doc/api/
# Generated native runners for the example fixture — android/, ios/ and macos/
# are ALL tracked (Nico, 2026-08-05). This reverses the earlier "only macos/ is
# tracked; ios/ is regenerated on demand" rule: the fixture is what the gauntlet
# runs on real hardware, so a device run must not depend on one machine having
# happened to `flutter create` the right platform. Tracking them is what makes
# the run reproducible from a clean checkout.
#
# Cost, measured before the change: the platform runners add ~240 KB (ios/) to
# the published leonard_flutter archive, which stayed at 15 MB with android/
# already tracked. Each runner keeps its own .gitignore, so build output and
# Pods stay out.
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
/build/
/coverage/

# Symbolication related
app.*.symbols

# Obfuscation related
app.*.map.json

# Android Studio will place build artifacts here
/android/app/debug
/android/app/profile
/android/app/release
